OpenRouter
OpenRouter ( https://openrouter.ai/?utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+Apr=
il+2026&utm_content=3DA1+Welcome&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcus=
tomer.io )

=E2=80=83

Hi Patrio Gabriel,

Welcome to OpenRouter. You now have one API key that reaches 300+ models ac=
ross OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Meta, DeepSeek, xAI, Mistral, and every oth=
er major provider. It is drop-in compatible with the OpenAI SDK, so the int=
egration looks identical to what you already have, and you stop maintaining=
 a separate account and a separate SDK for each provider.

Create your API key ( https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys?utm_source=3Demai=
l&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm_content=3Dwelcome=
&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+2026&utm_content=3DA1+Welcome&ut=
m_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcustomer.io )

=E2=80=83

One key, one billing surface, one rate limit pool, one place to see usage. =
When a provider has a bad hour, OpenRouter falls over to the next provider =
serving the same model, so your app does not cascade failures when OpenAI o=
r Anthropic goes down. When a new model drops, it is a string change, not a=
n integration project.

Getting Started

1. Create your API key ( https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys?utm_source=3Dc=
ustomerio&utm_medium=3Demail&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm_content=3Dche=
cklist&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+2026&utm_content=3DA1+Welc=
ome&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcustomer.io )

2. Point the OpenRouter SDK at openrouter.ai/api/v1

3. Make your first request ( https://openrouter.ai/docs/quickstart?utm_sour=
ce=3Dcustomerio&utm_medium=3Demail&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm_content=
=3Dchecklist&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+2026&utm_content=3DA=
1+Welcome&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcustomer.io )

SWITCHING MODELS

Switch from openai/gpt-4o-mini to anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6 to openrouter=
/auto by changing one string in your API call. No new SDK, no new credentia=
ls, no second billing account. Browse all 300+ models ( https://openrouter.=
ai/models?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboardi=
ng_v2&utm_content=3Da1_models_link&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+Apri=
l+2026&utm_content=3DA1+Welcome&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcust=
omer.io ).

openrouter/auto is worth knowing from day one. It reads the prompt and pick=
s a model per request, so you can ship without committing to a specific pro=
vider. Roughly 63 percent of auto traffic routes to models under $1 per mil=
lion tokens, which is how simple prompts stop hitting expensive models. See=
 how auto-routing works ( https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/routing/routers=
/auto-router?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboa=
rding_v2&utm_content=3Da1_auto_routing_link&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+=
-+v4+April+2026&utm_content=3DA1+Welcome&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_sour=
ce=3Dcustomer.io ).

